Article 4 The written application shall state the following:
(1) The name, sex, age, work unit, and address of the applicant;
(2) The court of which country rendered the judgment, and the outcome and date of the judgment;
(3) The circumstances of service and appearance before the court;
(4) The grounds and request for the application;
(5) Other matters that need to be stated.

Article 12 Upon examination, if a foreign divorce judgment falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall not be recognized:
(1) The judgment has not yet taken legal effect;
(2) The foreign court that rendered the judgment has no jurisdiction over the case;
(3) The judgment was rendered in the absence of the defendant who had not been lawfully summoned;
(4) A divorce case between the same parties is being tried by a Chinese court or has been adjudicated, or a divorce judgment between the same parties rendered by a third country court has already been recognized by a Chinese court;
(5) The judgment violates the fundamental principles of Chinese law or endangers the national sovereignty, security, and social public interests of China.
